# Laptop Exec - SSH-First (hybrid on Windows)

`~/mounts/` is optional SSHFS (may be STALE). Do not ask to enable SSHFS.

## Hybrid routing (read this first)

On **Windows** when Cursor MCP `windows-mcp` / `user-windows-mcp` is **ready**:

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| File read/write/list/info | **windows-mcp `FileSystem`** (absolute Windows path under project root) |
| Shell / build / tests | **windows-mcp `PowerShell`** (fallback: `laptop-exec run`) |
| Screenshot / Click / Type / UI | **windows-mcp only** |
| `git` | **`laptop-exec git` only** |
| Content search | **`laptop-exec rg` only** (MCP search ≠ content grep) |
| Mac / MCP down | **`laptop-exec` only** |

Do **not** default every file I/O to `laptop-exec` when MCP is ready. Keep laptop-exec forever for git/rg/Mac/fallback — never uninstall it.

**Speed:** On Windows+MCP, fan out **~8 parallel** `windows-mcp` `FileSystem` (and PowerShell) calls in one turn to fetch many files fast. MCP has no SSH mux limit. Reserve the ≤4 / hard-cap-8 parallelism advice for **`laptop-exec` only** (shared ControlMaster slots).

## No trial-and-error

Hooks deny on `/mounts/`: Read, Write, Edit, EditNotebook, StrReplace, Delete, Grep, Glob, and heavy Shell. Deny is **expected**. **Do not retry.** First allowed I/O = windows-mcp (hybrid table) **or** Shell + `laptop-exec`. Project `hooks.json` must stay `{"version":1,"hooks":{}}`.

| Denied | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Read | windows-mcp `FileSystem` when ready; else `laptop-exec read -p ID REL` |
| Write/Edit/StrReplace | windows-mcp `FileSystem` write when ready; else `laptop-exec write -p ID REL` |
| Grep/Glob | `laptop-exec rg -p ID PATTERN [pathspec]` (**not** MCP) |
| heavy Shell | windows-mcp `PowerShell` when ready; else `laptop-exec git\|run\|rg\|read -p ID …` |

**rg is NOT ripgrep:** never `-i`/`-l`/`-n`/`--glob` (rejected; old hangs). Pathspecs only.

**Task spawn is ALWAYS allowed.** Every Task `prompt` MUST paste the SSH-first block from the `laptop-exec` skill (`-p ID`; no Read/Grep on mounts; no `rg -i/--glob`; hybrid note). Prefer ~8 parallel windows-mcp FileSystem when hybrid; ≤4 parallel `laptop-exec` (hard cap 8 SSH slots). On deny, run `NEXT:`.

Both flag orders: `laptop-exec -p ID read REL` and `laptop-exec read -p ID REL`.

## Paths / boot

- Repo-relative only for laptop-exec — never `/home/$USER/mounts/ID/...`
- windows-mcp paths: absolute Windows under project root (from `LAPTOP_REMOTE_PATH` / mount `REMOTE_PATH` + REL; not Desktop-relative)
- Windows `laptop-exec read` may mojibake non-ASCII; `write` is binary-safe
- `laptop-exec status` → DOWN => user `connect.bat/sh`; STALE mount + UP tunnel => still use laptop path (MCP or LE)
- Resolve project: `-p` > workspace env/`PWD` under mounts > `ACTIVE_MOUNT`

## Allowed without laptop-exec

`/tmp/**`, `~/.cursor/**`, non-mount paths; light shell (`echo`, `ls`, `python3`); any command containing `laptop-exec`; Cursor MCP `windows-mcp` tools when that server is ready.

## Mux / sudo

8 session slots; shared ControlMaster; do not stress-test the tunnel. Sudo: `sudo-from-laptop --smart|--sepidz -- …` — never ask for a password.
